# Prospective textarea coordinate correction

Source preparation only, pending immutable independent negative proof. Author573+manifest and source-only plan44 remain untouched. Root authorized a separate correction epoch after Automation freezes its actual Chrome failure/control. No candidate code copy, app/test/browser/original/benchmark action has run in this folder.

Confirmed independent observation: saved `😀 lead\r\nneedle here\r\nsecond needle\r\n`, released candidate client67150d5e, source result start9/end15 at line2. Native textarea value normalizes CRLF to LF; selecting raw source offsets highlights `eedle ` instead of `needle`. This is a saved-source versus DOM coordinate error; it does not change disk bytes or original backend positions. Literal current-production control must remain a separately pinned source epoch. It does not retroactively invalidate earlier unrelated LF/first-line browser observations or make earlier modeled tests native-browser proof.

Narrow planned change: retain revision/draft/search/open/mounted checks; additionally require the text currently shown to equal CRLF/bare-CR→LF normalization of the exact saved source string, validate finite integer source offsets and refuse a coordinate inside CRLF. Count collapsed CRLF pairs before each source endpoint, then select the corresponding native textarea UTF-16 interval. Bare CR changes character value to LF but not length; astral characters retain two UTF-16 code units. Use inline trusted fixed normalization/linear mapping, avoiding a new static import route and avoiding untrusted main-thread regex. Any incompatible shown text refuses navigation, rather than guessing.

Predeclared finite controls: literal and regex second/later line navigation with multiple CRLFs; astral text before/within match; bare CR, LF, CRLF and mixed endings; same-line non-ASCII and combining characters; zero-length lookahead/endpoints; invalid/inside-pair/out-of-range rows; dirty draft, changed exact revision, shown-text mismatch, held query/option/read generations, Close and disposed state, held Save while typing. Preserve backend row positions/revisions/disk bytes and all existing worker resources. No change to original32/918 backend comparison source bodies and no new original execution needed unless a real matching-source change occurs.

The former regex UI fixture is a custom model whose value field did not normalize CRLF. A faithful textarea model and adjusted expected DOM values/selection indices are required in the new test epoch; exact old573 bodies/results must stay historical, with explicit source-level adapter/difference records. Do not add fallback branches or claim an unmodified old UI body exercises native textarea behavior. Actual corrected browser acceptance needs an independent re-review and a separately authorized private campaign.
